+# Robot Fire Dataset v1 Pipeline
+
+This pipeline generates aligned robot-vision samples from the InteriorGS office
+scene and FieryGS native fire simulation. It does not train a robot model.
+
+## Frozen production profile
+
+- `source_mode = native_reignite`
+- legacy clipped `XYZ2RGB`
+- `hdr_aces = false`
+- `strength = 0.005`
+- `smoke_strength = 0.2`
+- native Phong illumination enabled
+- coarse/fine volume samples: `64 / 512`
+- deterministic seed: `42`
+
+Experimental source modes remain in the repository but are not used by Dataset v1.
+
+## Dataset design
+
+- Nine scenarios: Table, Sofa, Curtain × LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH.
+- Fifteen physical states per scenario: three each from IGNITION, EARLY,
+  ESTABLISHED, SPREAD, and LATE.
+- Eight fixed Go2-like first-pass cameras per state.
+- Expected total: `9 × 15 × 8 = 1080` samples.
+- Cameras from the same simulation state always share one train/validation/test split.
+
+## Output layout
+
+Dataset root: `D:\interiorgs_data\office_01\robot_fire_dataset_v1`
+
+- `rgb/`: lossless production RGB PNG
+- `depth/`: uint16 solid-scene depth PNG in millimetres; zero is invalid
+- `semantic/`: compressed NPZ with Gaussian, instance, part, material, and burnability maps
+- `fire_masks/`: float32 contribution NPY and binary PNG
+- `smoke_masks/`: float32 contribution NPY and binary PNG
+- `metadata/samples/`: per-sample camera, physics, renderer, and QA metadata
+- `cameras/`: camera intrinsics, extrinsics, and generation QA
+- `manifests/`: scenario, sample, and grouped split manifests
+- `reports/`: generation, completeness, statistics, and review reports
+
+Fire and smoke masks are generated from their volumetric ray-marching
+contributions. They are never inferred from RGB colors.
+
+## Resumable production command
+
+Run from the FieryGS repository with the `fire_gaussian_win` Python executable:
+
+```powershell
+& 'D:\anaconda\envs\fire_gaussian_win\python.exe' -m adapter.fire_dataset.run_dataset_v1_pipeline --phase all --resume
+```
+
+The command first skips the three complete HIGH simulations, creates the six
+missing LOW/MEDIUM production simulations, extracts physical states, writes the
+1080-sample manifest, and renders incomplete samples. Re-running the same command
+with `--resume` skips complete samples.
+
+## Post-generation summary
+
+```powershell
+& 'D:\anaconda\envs\fire_gaussian_win\python.exe' -m adapter.fire_dataset.summarize_dataset_v1
+```
+
+This writes `reports/DATASET_V1_REPORT.md`, `dataset_v1_stats.json`, and a
+non-destructive visual review list. Dataset v1 completion does not authorize
+YOLO, segmentation, domain-adaptation, or ROS training.
