+++ b/adapter/fire_native_parity/METRIC_GRID_LIMITATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Metric Grid Limitation
+
+The released FieryGS solver stores the scene voxel size in configuration, but
+`FireSolver` still sets `dx = 1.0` and derives its finite differences and time
+step from that normalized cell size. Therefore changing the InteriorGS voxel
+grid from 5 cm to 2.5 cm alone would double the metric resolution without
+performing a physically comparable simulation.
+
+A metric-aware redesign must pass physical `dx` into the solver and revisit:
+
+- `dt` and the CFL/stability constraints of velocity and scalar advection;
+- Laplacian factors (`1 / dx²`) in heat diffusion and viscosity;
+- gradient, divergence, curl, and pressure-projection scaling;
+- the conversion between cell velocity and metres per second;
+- buoyancy acceleration and how it integrates over the new `dt`;
+- per-material thermal diffusivity in physical units rather than a global
+  normalized multiplier;
+- boundary thickness, ignition dimensions, and all thresholds currently
+  expressed in voxel counts;
+- regression tests that compare the same metric scene at multiple resolutions.
+
+This is a medium-to-high engineering-cost solver change: roughly one to two
+weeks for implementation and unit/regression tests, followed by validation
+against a known physical or synthetic reference. It is intentionally not
+implemented in this native-feature recovery task.
