@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# Room-scale Fire Scenario Layer
+
+## Reused interfaces
+
+- `common.load_scenario(path)` validates YAML and normalizes the legacy schema.
+- `generate_ignition.py` resolves semantic instance IDs to exact Gaussian rows.
+- `material_voxel_builder.py` provides the shared room grid, Gaussian-to-voxel mapping,
+  material grid, and confirmed-combustible occupancy. It is built once per scene.
+- `fuel_initializer.py` converts an exact ignition mask into FieryGS configuration and
+  traceable initialization assets.
+- `run_scenario_solver.py` instantiates the native `simulation.fire_main.FireSolver` and
+  exports the active double buffers.
+- `validate_initialization.py`, `validate_smoke_test.py`, and
+  `validate_fire_render.py` provide dry-run, physical-state, and RGB validation.
+- `tools/render_material_fire_video.py` calls the unchanged native
+  `gaussian_renderer.renderer_with_fire.render_fire`.
+
+## Room scenario data flow
+
+`YAML + seed -> semantic object Gaussians -> object-owned exposed surface voxels -> exact
+ignition mask -> propagation occupancy -> native FireSolver -> native render_fire`
+
+Ignition sources and propagation candidates are separate. Only voxels in the exact
+ignition mask are hot at frame zero. The shared combustible voxel grid controls what may
+ignite later.
+
+## Exact-mask compatibility boundary
+
+The upstream solver accepts one axis-aligned `ignition_box`. A box cannot represent
+multiple separated patches without heating intervening or neighbouring objects. The
+adapter therefore stores `ignition_voxel_mask.npy` and `run_scenario_solver.py` initializes
+the native solver's wood-temperature field from it. No combustion, heat transfer, fluid,
+or rendering kernel is changed. A bounding box is still emitted for diagnostics and
+legacy compatibility, but batch scenarios use the exact-mask adapter path.
+
+## Fire levels
+
+LOW, MEDIUM, and HIGH alter physical initial conditions and requested duration: exposed
+surface-layer depth, patch count, target initial hot-voxel count, and simulation frames.
+They do not alter solver constants or renderer brightness. The first comparison uses one
+shared render configuration.
+
+## Reproducibility and outputs
+
+Every scenario records its YAML, seed, source paths, Gaussian count, exact voxel
+coordinates, initial non-target count, propagation candidates, and timestamps. Existing
+validated experiments under `fire_scenarios/` remain immutable; room-batch results live
+under `D:/interiorgs_data/office_01/fire_scenarios_batch/`.
