@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+# Bounded solid-to-gas source validation
+
+Production rendering remains frozen at the accepted legacy path (`XYZ2RGB` clipping,
+`hdr_aces=false`, `strength=0.005`, `smoke_strength=0.2`). No fire renderer or solver
+sampling changes were made.
+
+The 60-frame comparison covered `initial_only`, native `native_reignite`, and bounded
+surface sources at eta 0.3/0.6/1.2. All runs completed on CUDA with active-buffer
+export verification and finite arrays. The bounded source produced a localized source
+region around the table, with no global/upward injection. Eta=1.2 was selected for the
+120-frame continuation because it is the strongest bounded candidate under the stated
+caps (`source_max_per_solid=0.05`, `source_max_per_air=0.2`, total emergency limit 100).
+
+The occupancy proxy is monotone: over 120 frames the table occupancy decreased from
+51,559.69 to 51,457.90 (loss 101.79), with zero negative-loss voxels. This is a
+diagnostic availability/consumption proxy, not a calibrated mass model.
+
+The 120-frame eta=1.2 run completed with source diagnostics and flow diagnostics. It
+is suitable as the bounded-source physics candidate for subsequent visual inspection;
+do not start a longer run until the rendered plume and source localization are reviewed.
